WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.255
Communication and documentation run through the entire incident response lifecycle.

2
00:00:04.405 --> 00:00:09.512
They are how teams keep technical work, business decisions, and accountability aligned.

3
00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:15.619
Useful records include timelines, evidence references, affected assets, owners, decisions made, approvals, actions taken,

4
00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:17.969
open questions, and known assumptions.

5
00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:20.319
Different audiences need different detail.

6
00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:23.448
Analysts may need log references and hypotheses.

7
00:00:23.598 --> 00:00:27.002
Executives may need impact, risk, and next decisions.

8
00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:32.684
Legal and privacy teams may need data categories, notification considerations, and preservation status.

9
00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:36.238
System owners need practical recovery and validation steps.

10
00:00:36.388 --> 00:00:38.941
Good communication is clear about uncertainty.

11
00:00:39.091 --> 00:00:45.474
It should not overstate what the team knows, and it should not hide material risk.

12
00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:49.454
Lessons learned are the bridge from response to improvement.

13
00:00:49.604 --> 00:00:57.264
A post-incident review should identify what worked, what slowed the team down, which detections or logs were missing,

14
00:00:57.414 --> 00:01:02.520
whether access or backups behaved as expected, and what playbooks need updates.

15
00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.870
The goal is not blame.

16
00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:13.531
The goal is a concrete improvement plan with owners, deadlines, and evidence that the organization will be better prepared next

17
00:01:13.681 --> 00:01:15.881
time.

18
00:01:16.031 --> 00:01:21.137
Documentation should be written as the response unfolds, not reconstructed entirely afterward.

19
00:01:21.287 --> 00:01:28.521
Time stamps, decision owners, evidence locations, and open questions are much easier to capture in the moment.

20
00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:35.054
Clear notes also protect the team from confusion when shifts change, leaders ask for updates,

21
00:01:35.204 --> 00:01:39.460
or a later review examines why a decision was made.
